IMPORT prelude

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Cth) -- how many flexible PPL days there are for a child and how many one partnered claimant may
-- take (ss 11D, 31AB(2), (3), 31ABA), the cap on days paid to both parents at once (s 21), who may claim (s 54) and what a claimant
-- other than the birth mother needs from her (s 13(2)(b), (d), (3), s 15), eligibility on a day (s 31AA(2)), the work test
-- (ss 32-36A), paid work and the self-employed (s 35), the income test and its limits (ss 37, 40, 41), the Australian residency
-- test (ss 45, 46) and the newly arrived resident's waiting period (s 31A), when to claim (s 60), the instalment and its amount
-- (ss 63, 65), the continuous flexible period (s 71A), who pays -- the employer as paymaster or the Secretary (ss 72, 73, 74,
-- 84, 101) -- and the PPL superannuation contribution (s 115C).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 48, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 57, 2025), register id
-- C2026C00294, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2010A00104.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0010 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 7 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c061 (2030-08-22, unpaid leave begins and PPL claimed: how many paid weeks, shared
-- how, paid by whom?), c063 (2030-09-05, Liam's reserved weeks: what is reserved, what may be transferred?), c071 (2033-04-12,
-- Ella born); Jake k052 (2033-01-22, is an unmarried mother eligible?), k053 (2033-01-22, is a self-employed father eligible,
-- married or not?); Daniel d040 (2030-02-02, Luca born, PPL shared), d04c (2034-04-14, Jarrah as paymaster of Chloe's PPL:
-- what must the employer do?). SCOPED to the provisions those events name, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions
-- needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Everything the PPL rules prescribe (exceptional circumstances claimants, s 31AA(4), (5) conditions, the
-- s 31AB(3)(d) and s 13(2)(d) carve-outs, what counts as paid work or paid leave) -- these are INPUTS; the national minimum
-- wage (set by a Fair Work Commission order, an INPUT); the indexed income limits after 1 July 2021 (individual) and 1 July
-- 2024 (family) -- INPUTS; "Australian resident", "partner" and "income support payment" (Social Security Act meanings, not
-- deposited) -- INPUTS; adjusted taxable income (Family Assistance Act Schedule 3) -- an INPUT; the SG charge percentage and the
-- nominal interest method -- INPUTS; adoption (Part 6-1), special PPL claims (s 14), stillbirth (s 31AA(3)), COVID-19
-- claimants (ss 19B, 33A, 34(1)(e), (f)), jobkeeper, multiple births (s 20), birth verification (s 18), the s 33(2A) work
-- cessation day, the s 46(4), (5) extensions, the waiting-period exemptions themselves (s 31A(6A)-(7A), an INPUT), review of
-- decisions, the instalment period and payday (s 64), PPL funding amounts beyond s 73, employer notices (s 82), debts, and civil
-- penalties.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. Adding 10000 gives the same day a year later (a 29 February birthday is not modelled).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 -- leave`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 11D -- flexible PPL days`

-- s 11D: "A day is a flexible PPL day for a child if the day occurs in the period that: (a) starts on the day the child is born;
-- and (b) ends on the day before the child's second birthday."
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is a flexible PPL day for the child` IF
        `the day` AT LEAST `born on`
    AND `the day` LESS THAN `born on` PLUS 20000

§§ `ss 31AB(2), (3), 31ABA -- how many days, and the reserved period`

-- s 31ABA(1), total limit in relation to the child: "(a) for a child born before 1 July 2024--100 flexible PPL days ...; (b) ...
-- between 1 July 2024 and 30 June 2025--110 ...; (c) ... between 1 July 2025 and 30 June 2026--120 ...; (d) for a child born on
-- or after 1 July 2026--130 flexible PPL days for the child."
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total flexible PPL days for the child` MEANS
    IF `born on` LESS THAN 20240701 THEN 100
    ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20250701 THEN 110
         ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20260701 THEN 120
              ELSE 130

-- s 31ABA(2), "Claimant limit when partnered--reserved period": 90, 100, 105, and "for a child born on or after 1 July 2026--110
-- flexible PPL days for the child". Note 2 to s 31ABA(1): "The difference between the number of days specified in this subsection
-- and the number of days specified in subsection (2) is reserved for other claimants (see section 31AB)."
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the partnered claimant's limit` MEANS
    IF `born on` LESS THAN 20240701 THEN 90
    ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20250701 THEN 100
         ELSE IF `born on` LESS THAN 20260701 THEN 105
              ELSE 110

GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days reserved for other claimants` MEANS
    `the total flexible PPL days for the child` `born on` MINUS `the partnered claimant's limit` `born on`

-- INFERENCE, not in the text: the scenarios count in weeks. The Act counts days; a continuous flexible period is made of "week
-- days" (s 71A), so five days to the week is used only to translate.
GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`in weeks of five week days` MEANS
    `days` DIVIDED BY 5

-- s 31AB(2): not eligible once determinations are in force "in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child
-- specified in subsection 31ABA(1)" (no exceptional circumstances). (3): not eligible if "(a) the relevant claimant has a partner
-- at the time the relevant claimant makes their first effective claim", (b) determinations for the claimant are in force for the
-- s 31ABA(2) number, (c) no exceptional circumstances, and "(d) the relevant claimant does not satisfy the conditions prescribed by
-- the PPL rules for the purposes of this paragraph". Whether a day paid to both parents at once counts once or twice toward
-- the child's total is not said; `days already paid for the child` is an INPUT that leaves that to the reader.
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER, `days already paid for the child` IS A NUMBER, `days already paid to the claimant` IS A NUMBER,
      `partnered at first claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the PPL rules conditions in s 31AB(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further days the claimant may be paid` MEANS
    IF `partnered at first claim` AND (NOT `meets the PPL rules conditions in s 31AB(3)(d)`)
    THEN `the greater of` 0 (`the lesser of`
                                (`the total flexible PPL days for the child` `born on` MINUS `days already paid for the child`)
                                (`the partnered claimant's limit` `born on` MINUS `days already paid to the claimant`))
    ELSE `the greater of` 0 (`the total flexible PPL days for the child` `born on` MINUS `days already paid for the child`)

§§ `s 21 -- days paid to more than one person`

-- s 21(1): the Secretary must not make a payability determination for a day if "(a) the effect of one or more payability
-- determinations ... is that parental leave pay is payable to more than one person for the same flexible PPL day for the child on a
-- total of: (i) if the child is born before 1 July 2025--10 flexible PPL days; or (ii) if the child is born on or after 1 July
-- 2025--20 flexible PPL days; and (b) ... parental leave pay is payable to another person for the relevant day." (2): the PPL rules
-- may prescribe days that do not count.
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the limit on days paid to both at once` MEANS
    IF `born on` LESS THAN 20250701 THEN 10 ELSE 20

GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER, `days already paid to both at once` IS A NUMBER, `another person is paid for the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21 bars the day` IF
        `days already paid to both at once` AT LEAST `the limit on days paid to both at once` `born on`
    AND `another person is paid for the day`

§§ `s 54 -- who may make a PPL claim`

-- s 54(1): "Only the following people can make a PPL claim for a child: (a) the child's birth mother; (b) an adoptive parent of the
-- child; (c) a person who: (i) is a parent of the child; and (ii) is not the child's birth mother; (d) the partner of the child's
-- birth mother; (e) the partner of an adoptive parent of the child; (f) the partner of a person covered by paragraph (c); (g) a
-- person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances". No paragraph asks
-- whether anyone is married. "partner" has the Social Security Act meaning (s 6), which was not deposited.
DECLARE Relationship IS ONE OF
    `the birth mother`
    `an adoptive parent`
    `a parent who is not the birth mother`
    `the partner of the birth mother`
    `the partner of an adoptive parent`
    `the partner of a parent who is not the birth mother`
    `a person in prescribed exceptional circumstances`
    `a grandparent caring for the child`

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A Relationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may make a PPL claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `a grandparent caring for the child` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 13(2)(b), (d), (3), 15 -- what a claimant other than the birth mother needs from her`

-- s 13(3) covers "(a) a person who: (i) is a parent (other than an adoptive parent) of the child; and (ii) is not the child's birth
-- mother; (b) the partner of the child's birth mother; (c) the partner of a person covered by paragraph (a)."
-- s 13(2)(b): for such a claimant, if "the child's birth mother has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child;
-- the child's birth mother satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made". (d): unless circumstances prescribed by
-- the rules apply, "(i) a permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(a)" (by the birth mother), "(ii) the
-- permission has not been revoked; and (iii) ... the number of flexible PPL days ... would not exceed the number of flexible PPL
-- days specified in the permission."
GIVEN `the relationship` IS A Relationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is covered by s 13(3)` IF
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `a parent who is not the birth mother` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the partner of the birth mother` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the partner of a parent who is not the birth mother` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A Relationship, `the birth mother has satisfied the work test` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the birth mother's permission is in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `days in the permission` IS A NUMBER,
      `days that would be payable to the claimant` IS A NUMBER, `the PPL rules disapply s 13(2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the birth mother conditions are met` IF
        (NOT (`the claimant is covered by s 13(3)` `the relationship`))
    OR  (    `the birth mother has satisfied the work test`
         AND (    `the PPL rules disapply s 13(2)(d)`
              OR  (`the birth mother's permission is in force` AND `days that would be payable to the claimant` AT MOST `days in the permission`)))

§§ `s 31AA(2) -- eligible on a day`

-- s 31AA(2): eligible on a flexible PPL day if "(a) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on that day; and (b) the person
-- is caring for the child on that day; and (c) on that day the person is performing no more than one hour of paid work; and (d) if
-- the person has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child--the person satisfies the work test
-- and the income test on that day; and (e) ... (i) the person satisfies the Australian residency test on the day the child was born;
-- (ii) if the day the child was born is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period ... subsection 31A(7) or (7A) applies".
-- s 31AA(1)(b) and s 31AB: and not ineligible -- (2), (3) the day caps (see `the further days the claimant may be paid`), (7)
-- "deceased on that day", (8) "that day is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period".
-- `married to the other parent` and `self-employed` are carried on the record and deliberately used by no rule: nothing in
-- Part 2-3 asks.
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `satisfies the residency test on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the residency test on the day of birth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caring for the child on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of paid work on the day` IS A NUMBER
    `previously satisfied the work and income tests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the work test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the income test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of birth is in an unexempted waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day is in an unexempted waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a day cap in s 31AB is reached` IS A BOOLEAN
    `deceased on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `married to the other parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is eligible on the day` IF
        `c`'s `satisfies the residency test on the day`
    AND `c`'s `caring for the child on the day`
    AND `c`'s `hours of paid work on the day` AT MOST 1
    AND (`c`'s `previously satisfied the work and income tests` OR (`c`'s `satisfies the work test` AND `c`'s `satisfies the income test`))
    AND `c`'s `satisfies the residency test on the day of birth`
    AND (NOT `c`'s `the day of birth is in an unexempted waiting period`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `the day is in an unexempted waiting period`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `a day cap in s 31AB is reached`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `deceased on the day`)

§§ `ss 32, 33, 36, 36A, 36AA -- the work test`

-- s 32 Step 4: "a period (a qualifying period) of 295 consecutive days in the work test period" of qualifying work or permissible
-- break; Step 5: "If the person has performed at least 330 hours of qualifying work in a qualifying period, the person satisfies
-- the work test." s 36A: also satisfied on premature birth or pregnancy complications "which prevented the person from performing
-- paid work", if the person would otherwise have satisfied it; s 36AA: special circumstances prescribed by the rules.
GIVEN `consecutive days in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER, `hours of qualifying work in it` IS A NUMBER,
      `s 36A applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `s 36AA applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person satisfies the work test` IF
        (`consecutive days in the qualifying period` AT LEAST 295 AND `hours of qualifying work in it` AT LEAST 330)
    OR  `s 36A applies`
    OR  `s 36AA applies`

-- s 33(1): "The work test period ... is the 392 days immediately before" (usually) "the day the child is born". s 33A: 600 days for
-- a COVID-19 affected claimant.
GIVEN `a COVID-19 affected claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the work test period in days` MEANS
    IF `a COVID-19 affected claimant` THEN 600 ELSE 392

-- s 36(2): "at least 1 day but not more than 84 consecutive days on which the person did not perform qualifying work" between two
-- qualifying work days is a permissible break.
GIVEN `days without qualifying work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gap is a permissible break` IF
        `days without qualifying work` AT LEAST 1
    AND `days without qualifying work` AT MOST 84

§§ `ss 34, 35 -- qualifying work and paid work, including the self-employed`

-- s 35(1): paid work is work "(whether as an employee, a contractor or otherwise ...) for another entity for remuneration"; (2)
-- "However, a person is taken not to perform paid work for the purposes of subsection (1) if the other entity is controlled by the
-- person"; (3) "Self-employed: A person performs paid work on a day if, on that day, the person performs work for the purposes of a
-- business that is carried on for profit ... by: (a) the person (whether alone or with others); or (b) an entity that is controlled
-- by the person".
GIVEN `works for another entity for remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN, `that entity is controlled by the person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `works for a for-profit business of the person or an entity the person controls` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person performs paid work` IF
        (`works for another entity for remuneration` AND (NOT `that entity is controlled by the person`))
    OR  `works for a for-profit business of the person or an entity the person controls`

-- s 34(1): qualifying work on a day if "(a) the person performs at least one hour of paid work; (b) the person takes a period of paid
-- leave of at least one hour; (ca) the day is a flexible PPL day for a previous child of the person and parental leave pay was
-- payable to the person on that day" (jobkeeper and COVID-19 payment periods not modelled).
GIVEN `hours of paid work` IS A NUMBER, `hours of paid leave` IS A NUMBER, `a paid PPL day for a previous child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is a qualifying work day` IF
        `hours of paid work` AT LEAST 1
    OR  `hours of paid leave` AT LEAST 1
    OR  `a paid PPL day for a previous child`

§§ `ss 37, 40, 41 -- the income test`

-- s 37: satisfied if "(1) ... the person's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year is not more than the relevant
-- individual PPL income limit"; or "(2) ... (c) the person does not have a partner at the time the person makes the claim ... and
-- (d) the person's adjusted taxable income ... is not more than the relevant family PPL income limit"; or "(3) ... (c) the person
-- has a partner ... and (d) the total of ... the person's adjusted taxable income ... [and] the adjusted taxable income of the
-- person's partner ... is not more than the relevant family PPL income limit". The three are alternatives.
GIVEN `own adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `has a partner when claiming` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `partner's adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `individual limit` IS A NUMBER, `family limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person satisfies the income test` IF
        `own adjusted taxable income` AT MOST `individual limit`
    OR  ((NOT `has a partner when claiming`) AND `own adjusted taxable income` AT MOST `family limit`)
    OR  (`has a partner when claiming` AND `own adjusted taxable income` PLUS `partner's adjusted taxable income` AT MOST `family limit`)

-- s 41(1): the individual PPL income limit is "(a) if the day is on or after 1 October 2010 but before 1 July 2021--$150,000"; then
-- the indexed amount (s 42, CPI -- an INPUT). (2): the family PPL income limit is "(a) if the day is on or after 1 July 2023 but
-- before 1 July 2024--$350,000"; then indexed from 1 July 2024 (an INPUT).
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `the indexed amount in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual PPL income limit` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST 20101001 AND `the day` LESS THAN 20210701 THEN 150000 ELSE `the indexed amount in force`

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `the indexed amount in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family PPL income limit` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST 20230701 AND `the day` LESS THAN 20240701 THEN 350000 ELSE `the indexed amount in force`

-- s 40: the relevant limits are those that apply "on the earlier of the following days: (a) the day the person made the claim; (b)
-- the day the child was born." s 39 fixes the reference income year by the same earlier day.
GIVEN `claimed on` IS A NUMBER, `born on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day that fixes the limits` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `claimed on` `born on`

§§ `ss 31A, 45, 46 -- residency and the waiting period`

-- s 45(1): the test is satisfied on a day if the person "(a) is an Australian resident; or (b) is a special category visa holder
-- residing in Australia; or (c) satisfies subsection (2)" (a visa holder determined under the Social Security Act). s 46(1):
-- "Despite section 45, a person does not satisfy the Australian residency test ... if ... the person has been absent from Australia
-- for more than 56 weeks since the day the person left Australia" (extensions in (4), (5) not modelled).
GIVEN `an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `a special category visa holder residing in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfies s 45(2)` IS A BOOLEAN, `weeks absent from Australia` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person satisfies the Australian residency test` IF
        (`an Australian resident` OR `a special category visa holder residing in Australia` OR `satisfies s 45(2)`)
    AND `weeks absent from Australia` AT MOST 56

-- s 31A(1)(b): a person who "becomes the holder of a permanent visa" (with exceptions) is subject to a newly arrived resident's
-- waiting period, which (2)-(4) end "when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks" after
-- its start. Its start depends on visa classes determined under the Social Security Act (an INPUT).
GIVEN `days in Australia since the waiting period began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the waiting period has ended` IF
    `days in Australia since the waiting period began` AT LEAST 104 TIMES 7

§§ `s 60 -- when to claim`

-- s 60: a claim "must be made in the period that: (a) starts on the day that is 97 days before the expected date of birth of the
-- child; and (b) ends on the day before: (i) if, before the child's first birthday, an effective claim for parental leave pay for
-- the child has been made by a PPL claimant for the child--the child's second birthday; or (ii) otherwise--the child's first
-- birthday."
GIVEN `days before the expected date of birth` IS A NUMBER, `the child's age in completed years` IS A NUMBER,
      `a PPL claimant claimed before the first birthday` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is made in time` IF
        `days before the expected date of birth` AT MOST 97
    AND (    `the child's age in completed years` LESS THAN 1
         OR  (`a PPL claimant claimed before the first birthday` AND `the child's age in completed years` LESS THAN 2))

§§ `ss 63, 65, 115C -- the instalment and the superannuation contribution`

-- s 65(2): "The daily national minimum wage amount for a day is 7.6 times the amount of the national minimum wage (when expressed as
-- a monetary amount per hour)". (1): an instalment is the sum of those amounts for each paid flexible PPL day in the instalment
-- period. The hourly national minimum wage is an INPUT.
GIVEN `hourly national minimum wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily national minimum wage amount` MEANS
    `hourly national minimum wage` TIMES 76 DIVIDED BY 10

GIVEN `hourly national minimum wage` IS A NUMBER, `paid days in the instalment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the instalment` MEANS
    `paid days in the instalment period` TIMES `the daily national minimum wage amount` `hourly national minimum wage`

-- s 115C(1): the contribution is "(a) the base contribution for the person for the year multiplied by the SG charge percentage for
-- that year; (b) the nominal interest rate amount". (2): the base contribution is the PPL funding amounts paid to the employer and
-- the instalments paid by the Secretary in the income year. (4): the SG charge percentage is the Superannuation Guarantee
-- (Administration) Act charge percentage "divided by 100" (an INPUT). The nominal interest method is in the rules (not modelled).
GIVEN `base contribution` IS A NUMBER, `SG charge percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PPL superannuation contribution before interest` MEANS
    `base contribution` TIMES `SG charge percentage` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `ss 71A, 101 -- the continuous flexible period and the employer determination`

-- s 71A: a continuous flexible period needs a period that "(b) ... only consists of consecutive flexible PPL days for the child that
-- are week days; and (c) ... consists of at least 40 consecutive flexible PPL days for the child that are week days", and it "ends
-- on the earlier of ... (i) the last day in the relevant period; (ii) the day before the child's first birthday." A period that
-- starts on or after the first birthday therefore cannot be one (an inference from (e)(ii)).
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER, `starts on` IS A NUMBER, `consecutive week days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period can be a continuous flexible period` IF
        `consecutive week days` AT LEAST 40
    AND `starts on` LESS THAN `born on` PLUS 10000

-- s 101(1): the Secretary must make an employer determination if satisfied that "(a)" a payability or initial eligibility
-- determination is in force; "(b) instalments are likely ... to be payable by the employer to the person for at least 40 consecutive
-- flexible PPL days that are week days; and (c) the person has, or will have, been employed by the employer for at least 12 months
-- immediately before" the expected date of birth (or, for a claim after the birth, the later of that and the birth); "(d) the
-- person has a continuous flexible period for the child and is likely to be an Australian-based employee"; "(da) there are no other
-- flexible PPL days prior to the person's continuous flexible period" paid or initially eligible; "(e) the employer has an ABN".
-- (2): (b) and (c) do not apply if the employer has elected under s 109 and the person consented in the claim. (3A): not if the
-- person "is receiving an income support payment". (4): the Secretary MAY decline (period ended, special claimant, child died,
-- another claimant's debt, employer not fit and proper). (1)(f), more than one employer, is not modelled.
DECLARE Employment HAS
    `a payability or initial eligibility determination is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive week days of instalments likely` IS A NUMBER
    `months employed immediately before the reference day` IS A NUMBER
    `has a continuous flexible period and is Australian-based` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier flexible PPL days were paid or initially eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer has an ABN` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer elected under s 109 and the person consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `receiving an income support payment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `e` IS A Employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Secretary must make an employer determination` IF
        `e`'s `a payability or initial eligibility determination is in force`
    AND (    `e`'s `the employer elected under s 109 and the person consented`
         OR  (    `e`'s `consecutive week days of instalments likely` AT LEAST 40
              AND `e`'s `months employed immediately before the reference day` AT LEAST 12))
    AND `e`'s `has a continuous flexible period and is Australian-based`
    AND (NOT `e`'s `earlier flexible PPL days were paid or initially eligible`)
    AND `e`'s `the employer has an ABN`
    AND (NOT `e`'s `receiving an income support payment`)

§§ `ss 72, 73, 74, 84 -- who pays, and what the paymaster must do`

-- s 72(1): "An employer must pay an instalment to a person on the payday for the instalment if: (a) the instalment is payable to the
-- person; and (b) an employer determination is in force for the employer and the person on a day during the instalment period ...;
-- and (c) as at the payroll cut-off for the instalment, the employer has been paid enough to fund the instalment." (1A): only for
-- days in the continuous flexible period. s 84(2): "The Secretary must pay an instalment that is payable to a person if the
-- Secretary ... never made an employer determination"; (2A) and for days outside the continuous flexible period.
DECLARE Payer IS ONE OF
    `the employer`
    `the Secretary`

GIVEN `an employer determination is in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day is in the continuous flexible period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Payer
`who pays the instalment for the day` MEANS
    IF `an employer determination is in force` AND `the day is in the continuous flexible period`
    THEN `the employer`
    ELSE `the Secretary`

-- s 73: "An employer has been paid enough to fund an instalment ... if the total of the PPL funding amounts paid to the employer for
-- the person for a child before that day is at least the total of ... (a) the amount of the instalments the employer has previously
-- paid ...; (b) the amount of the instalment; (c) the amount of any other instalment that is to be paid ... on the payday".
GIVEN `funding amounts received` IS A NUMBER, `instalments already paid` IS A NUMBER, `this instalment` IS A NUMBER,
      `other instalments due on the payday` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has been paid enough` IF
    `funding amounts received` AT LEAST `instalments already paid` PLUS `this instalment` PLUS `other instalments due on the payday`

GIVEN `payable` IS A BOOLEAN, `an employer determination is in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid enough at the payroll cut-off` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day is in the continuous flexible period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must pay the instalment on the payday` IF
        `payable`
    AND `an employer determination is in force`
    AND `paid enough at the payroll cut-off`
    AND `the day is in the continuous flexible period`

-- s 74: "must be paid in money by one, or a combination, of the following methods: (a) cash; (b) cheque, money order, postal order
-- or similar order, payable to the person; (c) the use of an electronic funds transfer system to credit an account held by the
-- person." (A civil penalty provision.) s 70 forbids other deductions (not modelled).
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `cash`
    `a cheque payable to the person`
    `electronic funds transfer to the person's account`
    `a set-off against a debt owed to the employer`
    `shares in the employer`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Method
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment method is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `a set-off against a debt owed to the employer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `shares in the employer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
